  "question": {
    "text": "A particle executes S.H.M. of amplitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis. At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, the position of the particle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> and it moves along positive <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis. The displacement of particle in time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#948;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, then the value <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#948;</mi></math> will be"
  },
